{
  "schema": "loom.graph_classes/1",
  "revision": 1,
  "calibration": true,
  "description": "Calibration example (R53, DUCH_GRAFU 0): a starting point the owner may reorder, hide, extend or replace through the graph_entry runtime-profile overlay; it is not a closed list. Inheritance applies to classes only; setting values do not inherit (they resolve through scopes). Wave 2 (GRAF_HUB_KOD_SILNIK §5-§7): classes declare `traits` (inherited along `parent`; a class id is also a trait of its own, so `requires: [\"message\"]` means \"is a message\"); a node may add traits of its own. Actions never appear here: an action fits an element when the element has the traits the action requires (data/runtime/actions.pack). `content` and `form` are separate nodes (§6): a form expresses a content (relation `expresses`, weight = fidelity); forms are subclassed per modality. `groups` are named trait bundles; the list is open. Devices (GRAF_HUB_KOD_SILNIK §4.3, S2/R9): the class `device` and its subclasses describe input/output devices; their instances and platform availability are in data/graph/devices.pack. `action_run` is the node of one run of an action; results hang on it (relation produced_by). Ports (GRAF_HUB_KOD_SILNIK §4, S2/R12): `port` is an abstract interface (asr, ocr, storage, llm ...), `adapter` one registered implementation of a port, `role_choice` the result of resolving a role of the `ports` profile (role, adapter, scope, source), `port_run` one real run through a port (ASR/OCR call, storage operation, ensemble outcome). Links: adapter `implements` port; role_choice `chose` adapter; port_run `produced_by` adapter, `derived_from` its inputs, `part_of` the action_run it happened in. Secrets appear only as references (secret key names), never as values.",
  "traits": {
